From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:47:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/35] =?UTF-8?q?Safarium:=20update=20from=20GitHub=20rele?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ases=20(Check=20for=20Updates=E2=80=A6)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Safarium > Check for Updates… reads the latest GitHub release
(v<version>-fix<N>) and compares it with SafariumBuild, which the
packaging script now stamps into Info.plist along with SafariumTag and
SafariumCommit. A newer release shows its notes with Install Update /
Remind Me Later / Skip This Version. Installing downloads the DMG with a
progress panel, checks the SHA-256 GitHub publishes for it, mounts it and
stages the app, then checks the staged app's bundle id, tag and code
signature. Safarium quits normally; a detached script waits for it to
exit, swaps the app in place (keeping the old one until the copy
succeeded) and relaunches it with --restore-last-session and this run's
own switches.

Packaged builds also check once a day (first a minute after launch) and
stay quiet unless a release the user hasn't skipped is out. Holding
Option turns the item into Install Local Build…, which installs the
newest *-local-*.dmg from ~/chromium/dist for builds that aren't
released. Test overrides: defaults SafariumUpdateFeedURL and
SafariumLocalUpdateDirectory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
